ra89r_re
========

Firmware reverse engineering and a custom firmware for the Retevis RA89R /
RA89G (TYT UV8800 / TH9000D family, Puya PY32F403).  See AGENTS.md.

This product includes software developed as part of the
UV-K1/K5V3 custom firmware project
(https://github.com/armel/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom, based on
https://github.com/DualTachyon/uv-k5-firmware), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).  Those files keep their original
copyright headers, and this list is where each imported file is recorded
progressively, as the RA89R port brings them in.

Imported from the UV-K1/K5V3 project
------------------------------------

| file | state | adaptation |
|---|---|---|
| `firmware/App/driver/bk4819.c` `.h` `bk4819-regs.h` | on `develop`, validated on the radio | transport is `rf_bus.c` (chip select `PB8`); local delay; two audio-path calls go through a registered callback; the four `gEeprom` reads became driver-local setters |
| `firmware/App/font.c` `font.h` | verbatim | none -- font tables (`gFontBig`, `gFontBigDigits`, `gFontSmall`, `gFont3x5`, `gFontSmallBold`) |
| `firmware/App/bitmaps.c` `bitmaps.h` | verbatim | none -- icon bitmaps |
| `firmware/App/driver/st7565.c` `.h` | adapted | same API and layout as the K1 (`gStatusLine[128]`, `gFrameBuffer[7][128]`, status line = page 0, frame lines = pages 1..7, `+4` column offset in `DrawLine`); the transport is this repo's bit-banged `driver/lcd_st7565.c` instead of the K1's hardware SPI, and the init is the bootloader-proven sequence |
| `firmware/App/ui/main.c` `.h` | verbatim | the VFO screen (`UI_DisplayMain`) and its helpers |
| `firmware/App/ui/menu.c` | verbatim | the menu screen (`UI_DisplayMenu`), the `MenuList[]` table, its sub-menu strings and its view/cursor state |
| `firmware/App/app/menu.c` `.h`, `app/action.c` `.h`, `app/common.h`, `app/generic.h`, `app/scanner.h`, `ui/battery.h`, `ui/welcome.h`, `driver/eeprom.h` | verbatim | the tables and headers the screens compile against |
| `firmware/App/version.c`, `App/dcs.c`, `App/frequencies.c`, `App/helper/battery.c` | verbatim | version strings, the CTCSS/DCS tables the menu indexes, the step/band tables, the battery arithmetic.  Their hardware calls (ADC, flash) are not reached by the screens yet |
| `firmware/App/ui/menu.h`, `ui/ui.h`, `ui/helper.c` `.h`, `ui/inputbox.c` `.h` | verbatim | menu table declarations, the screen dispatcher's interface, drawing/text helpers |
| `firmware/App/settings.h`, `radio.h`, `frequencies.h`, `dcs.h`, `functions.h`, `audio.h`, `misc.h`, `helper/battery.h`, `app/app.h`, `app/chFrScanner.h`, `app/dtmf.h`, `driver/system.h` | verbatim | the headers the screens compile against.  `settings.h` has one port addition: `PORT_SettingsDefaults()` |
| `firmware/App/driver/backlight.h` `.c` | extended | this repo's backlight driver plus the K1's names (`gBacklightCountdown_500ms`, `gBacklightBrightness`, `value[]`, `BACKLIGHT_InitHardware/_Update/_UpdateTickless/_SetBrightness`); the brightness is kept as state, the panel stays on -- the DAC dimming is not implemented |

| `firmware/App/py32f0xx.h`, `App/external/printf/printf.h` | shims | the vendor device header of the K1's PY32F071 and its embedded printf, mapped to this repo's `py32f4xx.h` and to newlib |
| `firmware/tools/host/py32f4xx.h`, `tools/host/host_hw.c` | test double | a host-only device header (CMSIS's `__DSB()` is ARM assembly, so a PC build cannot use the real one) plus stand-ins for the backlight and the two `BK4819_*` calls the screens make |

Not imported on purpose: the K1's `board.h`, `driver/{gpio,uart,systick}.h` and
its `driver/st7565.c` body stay this repo's; its `settings.c`, `radio.c`,
`misc.c` and the `app/*` modules are replaced for now by
`firmware/App/port_state.c`, whose stubs each name the K1 module that owns them.

Feature macros for the imported files live in `firmware/App/port_features.h` and
are force-included by the build (`-include`), so the imported sources stay
byte-comparable with upstream.
